{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}

{#
  ONE AWARD, PROMISED AND NOT YET ANNOUNCED.

  ── WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS AT ALL ─────────────────────────────────────────────

  `PublicResults` used to serve a result page as soon as the cycle's results date passed,
  announced or not. So a cycle still in `judging` published a full standing with a named
  winner and an index — from a panel that was still open, and with no sealed record behind
  it, which is why the page also printed "Recomputed under current rules". The gate is the
  announcement now: `results` or `archived`, written by `CycleMaterialiser` in the same
  transaction that crowns the winners and seals the standing.

  Which leaves the link. A result's URL is in front of people days before the date — in the
  congratulations mail, in the Pulse, in something forwarded — and whoever follows one on
  the day it was promised is exactly the person owed an explanation. A 404 there, on that
  day, reads as the result having been taken down.

  ── AND WHY IT DOES NOT LOOK LIKE AN ERROR ──────────────────────────────────

  Because nothing has gone wrong for the reader. The address is right, the award is real,
  and there is a true answer about it. It answers 200 with `noindex` — a crawler must not
  cache a holding page as this award's content, since the real result takes this same URL
  the moment it is announced.

  No countdown, no "check back soon", no invented date. The last date this platform named
  is the one it did not keep; naming a second one it has not earned is how a delay becomes
  the thing people remember about an award.
#}

{% block head_styles %}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  body[data-page="results"]{ background:#f0f2f2; color:var(--ag-ink); }

  .rl{ max-width:640px; margin:0 auto;
       padding:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,4.5rem) var(--ag-gutter,32px) clamp(3rem,8vw,5.5rem); }
  .rl-eyebrow{ margin:0 0 12px; font:600 var(--ag-fs-label) / 1 var(--ag-font-mono);
               letter-spacing:var(--ag-tracking-label); text-transform:uppercase;
               color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }
  .rl h1{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700;
          font-size:clamp(1.7rem,4.2vw,2.35rem); letter-spacing:-.02em; line-height:1.15; }
  .rl-lede{ margin:16px 0 0; font-size:16px; line-height:1.65; color:#3f484c; }
  .rl-rule{ height:1px; background:var(--ag-line-strong); margin:clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.2rem) 0; }

  /* The promised date, given the weight of a fact rather than of an apology. It is the
     thing a reader is holding this platform to. */
  .rl-date{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:4px 14px; align-items:baseline;
            padding:14px 16px; border-left:3px solid var(--ag-pulse);
            background:rgba(224,36,94,.05); }
  .rl-date dt{ margin:0; font:600 10.5px/1.4 var(--ag-font-mono); letter-spacing:.07em;
               text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }
  .rl-date dd{ margin:0; font-weight:600; font-size:15px; color:var(--ag-ink); }

  /* The operator's own words, set visibly apart from the platform's. A reader is entitled
     to know which sentences a person wrote for them and which the site derived. */
  .rl-note{ margin:20px 0 0; padding:16px 18px; border:1px solid var(--ag-line-strong);
            border-radius:var(--ag-r-lg); background:var(--ag-surface);
            font-size:15px; line-height:1.65; color:var(--ag-ink); white-space:pre-line; }
  .rl-note__k{ display:block; margin:0 0 8px; font:600 10.5px/1 var(--ag-font-mono);
               letter-spacing:.07em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); }

  .rl-body p{ margin:14px 0 0; font-size:15px; line-height:1.68; color:#4a5256; }
  .rl-acts{ display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px; margin:26px 0 0; }
  .rl-btn{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; min-height:44px; padding:0 22px;
           border-radius:var(--ag-r-pill); font-weight:600; font-size:14.5px;
           text-decoration:none; }
  .rl-btn--p{ background:var(--ag-green); color:#fff; }
  .rl-btn--g{ border:1px solid var(--ag-line-strong); color:var(--ag-ink); background:var(--ag-surface); }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="rl">
  <p class="rl-eyebrow">{{ late.programme }}{% if late.edition %} &middot; {{ late.edition }}{% endif %}</p>

  {# The award's own name, so somebody who followed a link is told which one they reached
     rather than only which edition it belongs to. #}
  <h1>{% if late.award %}{{ late.award }}{% else %}This award{% endif %} has not been
    announced yet</h1>

  <p class="rl-lede">The result for this award is <strong>late</strong>. Nothing has been
    decided, nothing has been withheld, and there is no winner to name yet.</p>

  <div class="rl-rule"></div>

  {# NAMED, not softened. A delay notice that will not repeat the date it broke is asking
     to be trusted twice. #}
  <dl class="rl-date">
    <dt>Was expected</dt>
    <dd>{{ late.promised|date('j F Y') }}</dd>
  </dl>

  {% if late.note %}
    <div class="rl-note">
      <span class="rl-note__k">From the organisers</span>{{ late.note }}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="rl-body">
    {# WHY the platform would rather be late, in the terms the rest of the site uses. A
       nominee reading this is owed the reasoning and not a reassurance. #}
    <p>An award here is published as one thing: every nominee who scored, the community
      support behind each of them, the panel&rsquo;s marks, and the denominator each share
      was measured against. It is announced once, and the standing is <strong>sealed</strong>
      at that moment so the figures a nominee is given are the figures this page shows for
      ever afterwards.</p>
    <p>That is why a part-finished result is not put up in the meantime. A figure that could
      still move is not a result, and announcing one twice would be worse for everybody
      named in it than announcing it late.</p>
    <p>This page becomes the result the moment it is announced &mdash; the address does not
      change, so a link already shared stays good.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="rl-acts">
    <a class="rl-btn rl-btn--p" href="/results">Awards already decided</a>
    <a class="rl-btn rl-btn--g" href="/awards">Awards running now</a>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
